    "note": "Metres are in the model's own axes (x right, z towards the camera in the S / single-direction sprite, y up; origin = the model pivot). anchor = the pixel (untrimmed frame, from top-left) where the footprint's ground centre is drawn: put it on the centre of the tiles the object covers (an even tile count puts it on a tile corner). Diamond tiles: u runs down-right, v down-left (Tiled isometric); square tiles: u right, v down. polygon = the ground collision polygon in frame pixels; tiles.polygon = the same polygon in tile units around the anchor. collision.source \"base\" = the hull of what stands on the ground (vertices below collision.cut metres above the bottom, e.g. a tree trunk); the whole model's hull is then canopy (canopyPolygon per direction), and footprint/tiles still cover the whole model. collision.rule says why: vehicle/building = always the whole hull; thin (trees, poles, lamps, signs) = the slice when it is at most half the hull; shape = the slice only under 15 % of the hull and near the middle; height = collisionHeight was given; asked = collision \"base\" or \"full\" was given."
